---
import CaseStudy from "../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro";
import manifestImage from "../../../Resource/Work/Manifest/Manifest_thumbnail_image.jpg?url";
---

<CaseStudy
  title="Manifest OS: Legal AI Tech"
  brand="Manifest OS"
  eyebrow="Manifest OS / Immigration law, done better"
  description="Rebuilding the case workflow for attorneys and paralegals — a design-system audit and a shipped AI assistant."
  role="Part-time Product Designer (Remote)"
  timeline="May 2026 – Current"
  team="Engineers, PMs, and 2 product designers"
  skills={["Cursor", "Claude Design", "Figma", "UX/UI"]}
  image={manifestImage}
  anchors={[
    { id: "overview", label: "Overview" },
    { id: "design-system", label: "Design System" },
    { id: "case-health", label: "Case Health" },
    { id: "ai-assistant", label: "AI Assistant" },
  ]}
>
  <div slot="intro">
    <p class="lede">
      Rebuilding the case workflow for attorneys and paralegals — a design-system
      audit and a shipped AI assistant inside an active legal-tech platform.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-stack">
    <div class="info-card">
      <h4>※ NDA note</h4>
      <p>
        Manifest OS is under active NDA — actual product screens can't be shown
        here. The sections below describe the contribution and outcomes; get in
        touch for a walkthrough of the real product.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="redacted-block" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="redacted">████████████████████████</span>
      <span class="redacted">████████████ ████████</span>
    </div>

    <div class="impact" data-impact>
      <div class="impact-col impact-col--results">
        <p class="impact-label">Achievement</p>
        <div class="impact-stats">
          <article class="impact-stat" data-impact-item>
            <p class="impact-stat-value">785 → 230</p>
            <p class="impact-stat-desc">Design tokens reduced (−70%)</p>
          </article>
          <article class="impact-stat" data-impact-item>
            <p class="impact-stat-value">~10k</p>
            <p class="impact-stat-desc">Daily users on the updated system</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="impact-col impact-col--contrib">
        <p class="impact-label">My contribution</p>
        <ul class="impact-list">
          <li data-impact-item>
            <strong>Design system</strong>
            <span>Audited and rebuilt the token scale for maintainability</span>
          </li>
          <li data-impact-item>
            <strong>Case Health Radar</strong>
            <span>Shipped and validated with attorney user testing</span>
          </li>
          <li data-impact-item>
            <strong>AI assistant</strong>
            <span>In-context chat and inline document editing in production</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="section-label" id="design-system">01 — Design System</p>
  <div class="split">
    <h3>Design system audit and rebuild</h3>
    <div class="content-div">
      <p class="prose-label">Method</p>
      <div class="tag-row">
        <span class="tag">Token Audit</span>
        <span class="tag">Storybook Sync</span>
        <span class="tag">Cursor</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Manifest's design system had grown past the point of being maintainable —
        hundreds of near-duplicate tokens for color, type, and spacing had
        accumulated as the product scaled. I audited the full token set and
        rebuilt it around a smaller, disciplined scale.
      </p>
      <p>
        Using Cursor to keep Storybook and the front end in sync with the new
        tokens, the updated system shipped to a platform used by roughly 10,000
        people daily.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="section-label" id="case-health">02 — Case Health Radar</p>
  <div class="split">
    <h3>At-a-glance case status for attorneys and PMs</h3>
    <div class="content-div">
      <p class="prose-label">Method</p>
      <div class="tag-row">
        <span class="tag">Prototyping</span>
        <span class="tag">Attorney Testing</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Shipped a feature that gives attorneys and PMs an at-a-glance read on
        where a case stands, iterated through several rounds of prototyping and
        validated directly with attorneys in user testing. One line of feedback
        that stuck: the tool would be a real asset for their team once it was
        fully deployed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="section-label" id="ai-assistant">03 — AI Assistant</p>
  <div class="split">
    <h3>AI assistant in the case detail page</h3>
    <div class="content-div">
      <p class="prose-label">Shipped</p>
      <div class="tag-row">
        <span class="tag">In-context Chat</span>
        <span class="tag">Inline Editing</span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Designed the in-context AI chat experience for the case detail page,
        along with AI-assisted inline document editing — both shipped to
        production.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</CaseStudy>
